+| `Rule30PeriodTwoOnset` | 2026-11-10 | Period 2: the column-`1` words of `Rule30PeriodTwoWidth5` and `Rule30PeriodTwoWidth6` from an explicit onset, for every history. If `H : Nat → Int → Bool` obeys rule 30 at the columns `1..b` (`Obeys`; nothing is assumed beyond them, and the configuration need not be finite) and column `0` alternates white, black on the `2 m` ticks `s, …, s + 2 m - 1`, then column `1` at the ticks `s + 2, …, s + 2 m` does not read a word of `col1Forbidden` of length `m` (`no_word5`, `no_word6`), nor at width `6` the word `101010000`, the listed `1010100001` without its last sample (`no_short6`). Two ticks from a white time move the window of the columns `1..b` by a double step whose only other inputs are two cells of column `b + 1` (`win_dstep`). One double step takes the `32` windows of width `5` onto `20` and the `64` of width `6` onto `38`, and both sets are closed under the double step (`img5_length`, `img6_length`, `img5_closed`, `img6_closed`). The kernel checks that no path from them reads a listed word, by layers of windows as in `Rule30GateTrapWords`, here with no entry time. So if column `0` alternates from `T` on, the words are excluded from every white time `t ≥ T + 2` (`onset5`, `onset6`), and for the single seed the kit's `col1_constraints` and `free_bit_constraints` hold with `T' = T + 2` (`col1_constraints5`, `col1_constraints6`, `free_bit_constraints5`, `free_bit_constraints6`). The free bits need the rule at column `0` and two more ticks (`free_bit5`, `free_bit6`). The onset is not claimed to be the earliest for actual configurations, and nothing here excludes period 2. Contributed by Gareth Herbert with Claude (Anthropic) and GPT (OpenAI), as Rule 30 Prize submission [PORTAL-ID](https://www.wolframcloud.com/obj/rule-30-prize/Agents/status/PORTAL-ID). | `win_dstep`, `img5_length`, `img6_length`, `img5_closed`, `img6_closed`, `no_word5`, `no_word6`, `no_short6`, `onset5`, `onset6`, `col1_constraints5`, `col1_constraints6`, `free_bit5`, `free_bit6`, `free_bit_constraints5`, `free_bit_constraints6` |
