 | `Rule30FourLeftSides` | 2026-11-04 | Every configuration with a leftmost black cell eventually agrees with one of four explicit strips on all left diagonals through wheel 87,866, with one common time shift (`left_side_classification`). The strips are realized by finite rows, no two are related by a time shift, and each configuration is on exactly one (`exactly_four_left_sides`, `on_exactly_one`). Equivalently, iterating `v ↦ 4 v ⊕ (2 v ∨ v)` modulo `2 ^ 87867` from any odd `v` reaches one of four numbers, each of least period 16 (`odd_reaches_one_of_four`, `least_period_16`). Extends `Rule30UniversalLeftSide`; the forks are Rowland's. Contributed by Gareth Herbert with Claude (Anthropic) and GPT (OpenAI). | `left_side_classification`, `exactly_four_left_sides`, `on_exactly_one`, `odd_reaches_one_of_four`, `least_period_16`, `seed_classified`, `four_distinct`, `fork_weights` |
